#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088875 :tutorial/content "Consider the circle with equation \n\n$$\n(x - 2)^2 + (y - 1)^2 = 3^2,\n$$\n\nas shown below. How can we calculate the points where the circle intercepts the $x$-axis?\n\n![](images/6b/6b80fa5fc106a8a78ba46e71ad8649da731a14777449b092f982e34138353b0a.png)\n\n  \n\nRemember, when the circle intercepts the $x$-axis, we must have $y = 0.$\n\nTherefore, to find the $x$-intercepts of the circle, we need to set $y = 0$ in the equation of the circle and solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(0-1)^{2} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+1 & =9 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =8 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{8} \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ x & =2\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle intercepts the $x$-axis at $(2-2\\sqrt{2},0)$ and $(2+2\\sqrt{2},0).$" :tutorial/id #uuid "34d31c83-a9c6-5d6b-83f8-8bb0c6633d79" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2441 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088876 :tutorial/content "Consider the circle with equation \n![](images/04/04942c0d9aa30a9c5730d1e16a580d9352f71ae539072e45a9c027f2c2a24e23.svg)\nas shown below. How can we calculate the points where the circle intercepts the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axis?\n\n![](images/9f/9f288ed4c4bf402576e0af193128e3a72866b4333be46b7cd7294e0e703cc8d4.png)\n\n \n\nWhen the circle intercepts the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axis, we must have ![](images/29/29da0a4605613d6a7fd9e7bb2f4fb45cbabe8a47109971682844cb222486a20c.svg)\n\nTherefore, to find the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-intercepts of the circle, we need to set ![](images/51/51a24269e3f466a9c7b886bcab70a365576b28534e323a55aec8b3ebe8d14571.svg) in the equation of the circle and solve for ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) as follows:\n\n![](images/c0/c0d3f8274a97b11ec1b29e9ac6f1594f153a558c54d40f3b0fe0a11cfc92ed34.svg)\n\nSo, the circle intercepts the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axis at ![](images/02/02009543b06c29977f90e4d9650dae5609d3dc21630daf575e791866a131b661.svg) and ![](images/80/809ca990d60556175140938d3a8f1c4a52048f8993899089f6f1dce4ea6b69aa.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "940d9cac-8606-5a8d-ba1a-d710d78c3a37" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2442 :tutorial/title "Calculating the Intersection of a Circle With the Y-Axis"}]}
